From: Husarion <support@husarion.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SHM: a regenerated listener keeps its new slot index

SharedMemManager::Listener::regenerate_port() builds a new Listener, whose
constructor registers it on the regenerated port and stores the new slot in
listener_index_, then move-assigns it into *this. The move assignment copied
the ring listener, the port and the manager but not listener_index_, so the
surviving listener kept writing its liveness status into its OLD slot on the
new segment. A participant that later takes that slot can die without the
port watchdog noticing (a survivor keeps the slot's counter moving): its ring
registration is never removed, the discovery port's ring fills, every push
fails ("Port full") while is_port_ok stays true, and new participants on the
host can no longer be discovered. Present in every release since 2.0.0
(checked: 2.6.x, 2.14.x, 3.0.0-3.6.2, master).

---
--- a/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemManager.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemManager.hpp
@@ -689,6 +689,7 @@
             other.global_listener_.reset();
             global_port_ = other.global_port_;
             other.global_port_.reset();
+            listener_index_ = other.listener_index_;
             shared_mem_manager_ = other.shared_mem_manager_;
             is_closed_.exchange(other.is_closed_);
 
